Z||000004||dman||09-19-2000||08:22 PM||||Hello everyone. Steve, try the search function that Cliff provided. It is awesome.<BR>Here's a few posts that discuss the 4.3 to help you get started. Only you can answer the question as to whether it is worth it or not. But if you do a search you'll find lots of info to help you make your decision.<P>4.3 Vortec in a Fiero? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004756.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004756.html</A> <P>4.3L install update (long)  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004874.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004874.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-19-2000||11:33 PM||||Thank's dman....<P> I can't get the search function to work, will try again tom.<BR> Thank's for the link's concerning the 4.3 motor swap...  <BR>dman,   what's your opinion on the swap?<BR>theorge....  what is your opinion??  <P>thanks steve||||reg||1
Z||000006||dman||09-20-2000||07:50 PM||||Steve, I think mrfixit58 described some of the pros/cons very well.<P>Since you can get the 4.3 for free, if the car that would be getting the new motor is not your daily driver, I'd do it in a heartbeat. Expect to spend more money and more time than you had originally planned. <P>This engine has lots of performance goodies, loads of low end torque (off the line, the car is gonna move!). Talk to squid (if possible), from what he's posted I suspect he is the only forum member (thus far) who has attempted a 4.3 conversion. I've heard descriptions of other people having done the conversion, but squid is the closest your gonna get to getting first hand info.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-21-2000||12:19 AM||||dman,  Thank You for your replies on this subject...<BR>AND Yes I want to put it in my 87GT which IS my daily driver<BR>But i could put it in my 85GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>That's what I want Low end torque.Dont we all...  <P>           Thank's...  Steve   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> 85GT 4.3 maybe||||reg||1
Z||000008||jlhuber||09-21-2000||01:31 PM||||just my $.02 worth of info.  i know a few people (including me) have wondered about the 4.3L conversion.  some people say that if you are going to go through that much trouble, just go ahead and do the SBC conversion.  to argue with that statement, if i can get a 4.3L for free, why would i buy a SBC just to get a few more HP?  i "acuired" a free 4.3L for free from a friend which i had planned on installing into my '86 gt.  unfortunately i had to sell my fiero **sniffle sniffle** so now i have a motor looking for a new donor car.  hey anyone 'round the tri-city michigan (midland, bay city, saginaw) area selling a formula that needs a motor?  anywho, if you are on a tight budget and can get a free motor, why not install it?  sorry for the rambling, but i am kinda bored ans spaced out sitting here at work.  dang, time to go back to lala land.||||reg||1
